# Sprint 1 — Logical Architecture for Release 1

**JIRA Story: Develop Release 1 Logical Architecture**

**Description:**  
Create the Release 1 logical architecture representing the major application and infrastructure components and their interactions. The architecture will serve as an input to threat modeling and detailed security design.

**Scope / Activities:**
- Document web/front-end components.
- Document application services and microservices.
- Document APIs and integration points.
- Document databases and storage services.
- Identify external/internal dependencies.
- Show major communication paths and trust boundaries.
- Identify authentication/authorization integration points where known.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- All Release 1 components are represented.
- Major interfaces and dependencies are documented.
- Component-to-component communication is identifiable.
- External integrations are captured.
- Architecture is reviewed with Engineering and Security.
- Diagram is available for threat-modeling activities.

---

**JIRA Story: Document Non-Functional Requirements for Document Management Service**

**Description:**  
Define the non-functional requirements necessary to establish the resilience, availability, recoverability, and performance expectations for the Document Management Service.

**Scope / Activities:**
- Define service availability/SLA requirements.
- Define Recovery Time Objective (RTO).
- Define Recovery Point Objective (RPO).
- Define Mean Time to Detect (MTTD) expectations.
- Define performance and scalability expectations.
- Identify backup/recovery requirements.
- Capture monitoring and operational expectations.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Availability target documented.
- RTO and RPO documented and agreed.
- MTTD/monitoring expectations documented.
- Performance/scalability requirements documented.
- Requirements reviewed with Architecture, Engineering, Product, and Security as applicable.

---

**JIRA Story: Define Data Classification and Data Flow for Release 1**

**Description:**  
Identify the data processed by the Document Management Service, assign appropriate classifications, and document how data moves through the Release 1 architecture.

**Scope / Activities:**
- Identify major data types processed/stored.
- Assign applicable data classifications.
- Identify sensitive/confidential data.
- Document data sources and destinations.
- Map data flows between application components.
- Identify data crossing trust/network boundaries.
- Identify data-at-rest and data-in-transit locations.
- Capture external/third-party data exchanges.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- Major data types are inventoried and classified.
- Sensitive data is clearly identified.
- Data Flow Diagram (DFD) completed.
- Data stores and processing locations are represented.
- Trust-boundary crossings are documented.
- External data exchanges are identified.
- DFD is usable as an input to threat modeling.

